[Chapter "Against ...Bf5"]
[Line "f3 and g4"]
[Opening "Rapport-Jobava System"]

{Against an early ...Bf5, White chases the bishop with pawns and gains space.} 1. d4 {Start with the queen's pawn.} 1... d5 2. Nc3 {The Jobava idea: the knight comes to c3 before the c-pawn moves, ready for Nb5 or e4.} 2... Nf6 3. Bf4 {Develop the bishop outside the pawn chain before e3.} 3... Bf5 4. f3 {Prepares g4 and controls e4.} 4... e6 5. g4 {Chase the bishop and grab space.} 5... Bg6 6. h4 {Threatens h5, trapping or chasing the bishop again.} 6... h6 {Black makes room on h7.} 7. e3 {Calm support for d4. White can follow with Qd2 and long castling.} *
